2. Kf6 { Now the king has occupied the key squares for the pawn on the 4th or even the 5th rank. Thus, the pawn could go that far, but there is an easier way. } Kh8 ( 2... Kh6 3. g5 Kh7 4. Kf7 ) 
 ( 2... Kg8 3. Kg6 Kf8 4. Kh7 { and the pawn's path is clear. } ) 
