 { So far, everything we have said is valid for all pawns with the exception of the rook's pawn, which deserves special attention. In a pawn ending, the rook's pawn is the most difficult to promote. It requires its path to be clear. The reason is the possibility of a stalemate when the pawn reaches the 7th rank supported by the king, no matter from where. This new situation renders useless all our rules about the range, the opposition and the key squares stated in the previous endings. In this position it doesn't matter who is to move: this is always a draw. } 1. Kh1 { White loses the opposition, but no matter: there is a stalemate. } h2 { Stalemate. Conclusion: With a rook's pawn, if the defender's king stands on the way, it is a draw. } 
 *

